        "created_at": 1794403707.614423
      },
      "rev_n_13_4c154d_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_13_4c154d_0",
        "node_id": "n_13_4c154d",
        "thought_text": "Instead of checking all pairs of semi-circles, we can sort the points first. Then, we only need to check if the current semi-circle intersects with the previous one or the one after it, reducing the number of checks.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-7436903988333783480",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794403836.689121
      },
      "rev_n_14_a40177_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_14_a40177_0",
        "node_id": "n_14_a40177",
        "thought_text": "We can use a sweep line algorithm where we maintain a set of active semi-circles. As we process each point, we add the corresponding semi-circle to the set and check for intersections with existing ones.",
